<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Full eigenvector pre-training pipeline</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide a broad algorithmic outline of eigenvector pre-training process in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ A.1 Full eigenvector pre-training pipeline ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Learning Laplacian Eigenvectors: a Pre-training Method for Graph Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Structure-Informed Graph Pre-training Framework</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            Graph <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math>; node features <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\{x_{j}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\{x_{j}\}</annotation></semantics></math>; training labels <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>; untrained Base GNN; untrained Downstream Prediction Head

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            Trained Base GNN and Downstream Prediction Head

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{X}\leftarrow\textsc{AugmentFeatures}(G,X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">AugmentFeatures</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{X}\leftarrow\textsc{AugmentFeatures}(G,X)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">BaseGNN</span> <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow\textsc{EigvecPreTrain}(G,\tilde{X},\textsc{BaseGNN})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">EigvecPreTrain</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">BaseGNN</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow\textsc{EigvecPreTrain}(G,\tilde{X},\textsc{BaseGNN})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;\text{Fine-tuning Epochs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mtext>Fine-tuning Epochs</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;\text{Fine-tuning Epochs}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{z}_{0},\dots,\vec{z}_{n}\leftarrow\textsc{BaseGNN}(G,\tilde{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">BaseGNN</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{z}_{0},\dots,\vec{z}_{n}\leftarrow\textsc{BaseGNN}(G,\tilde{X})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{Z}\leftarrow[\vec{z}_{1},\dots,\vec{z}_{n}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{Z}\leftarrow[\vec{z}_{1},\dots,\vec{z}_{n}]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{Y}\leftarrow\textsc{DownstreamHead}(\vec{Z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">DownstreamHead</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{Y}\leftarrow\textsc{DownstreamHead}(\vec{Z})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{Loss}=\textsc{LossCriterion}(\hat{Y},Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Loss</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">LossCriterion</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{Loss}=\textsc{LossCriterion}(\hat{Y},Y)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
              Backpropagate Loss, update model weights

</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <span id="alg2.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">BaseGNN, DownstreamHead</span>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Loss function</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Eigenvector loss, per-vector form:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{eigvec}=\frac{1}{k}\sum_{i=1}^{k}\lVert L\hat{u}_{i}-\lambda_{i}\hat{u}_{i}\rVert" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{eigvec}=\frac{1}{k}\sum_{i=1}^{k}\lVert L\hat{u}_{i}-\lambda_{i}\hat{u}_{i}\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Eigenvector loss, matrix form:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{eigvec}=\frac{1}{k}\lVert(L\hat{U}-\hat{U}\Lambda_{k})\rVert" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{eigvec}=\frac{1}{k}\lVert(L\hat{U}-\hat{U}\Lambda_{k})\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Energy loss, per-vector form:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{energy}=\frac{1}{k}\sum_{i=1}^{k}\hat{u}_{i}^{\top}L\hat{u}_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{energy}=\frac{1}{k}\sum_{i=1}^{k}\hat{u}_{i}^{\top}L\hat{u}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Energy loss, matrix form:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{energy}=\frac{1}{k}\Tr(\hat{U}^{\top}L\hat{U})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{energy}=\frac{1}{k}\Tr(\hat{U}^{\top}L\hat{U})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Energy loss is order-invariant and rotation invariant (see <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Energy and eigenvector losses are sign and basis invariant ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Learning Laplacian Eigenvectors: a Pre-training Method for Graph Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>); for applications in clustering, this is reasonable. However, we would like the model to learn the eigenvectors in their specific order, so we also define <span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">absolute energy loss</span>, matching the Rayleigh quotient with the ground-truth eigenvalue:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{energy\_abs}=\frac{1}{k}\sum_{i=1}^{k}\lvert\hat{u}_{i}^{\top}L\hat{u}_{i}-\lambda_{i}\rvert" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{energy\_abs}=\frac{1}{k}\sum_{i=1}^{k}\lvert\hat{u}_{i}^{\top}L\hat{u}_{i}-\lambda_{i}\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">This can be written as, in matrix form:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{energy\_abs}=\frac{1}{k}\Tr\lvert\hat{U}^{\top}L\hat{U}-\Lambda_{k}\rvert" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{energy\_abs}=\frac{1}{k}\Tr\lvert\hat{U}^{\top}L\hat{U}-\Lambda_{k}\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In practice, we do not show any results using absolute energy loss, and instead linearly combine energy loss with eigenvector loss to avoid order and rotation invariance. However, absolute energy loss remains an interesting avenue to explore.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.1 </span>Orthogonality</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure the model does not output <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> copies of the trivial eigenvector, we must give the model orthogonality constraints on the output vectors. There are again two reasonable choices here: <span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1) forced orthogonality</span> and <span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2) orthogonality loss</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Forced orthogonality</span>, used in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>, imposes orthogonality on the final outputs of the model via QR decomposition. In other words, if <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{U}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{U}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is the initial output to the model, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is an <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times k</annotation></semantics></math> matrix with orthonormal columns, and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\times k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\times k</annotation></semantics></math> upper triangular matrix, then we achieve the final output <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{U}</annotation></semantics></math> as such:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QR=\hat{U}^{\prime}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QR=\hat{U}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{U}=Q" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{U}=Q</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Orthogonality loss</span>, used in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite> imposes a softer constraint, encouraging orthogonality by penalizing the model for producing pairwise similar vectors. This can be written as:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{ortho}=\frac{1}{k}\lVert\hat{U}^{\top}\hat{U}-I\rVert" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{ortho}=\frac{1}{k}\lVert\hat{U}^{\top}\hat{U}-I\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Based on preliminary testing, we found that forced orthogonality improved performance on the eigenvector-learning, and thus use forced orthogonality in all of our experiments.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Energy and eigenvector losses are sign and basis invariant</h3>

<section id="A1.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.3.1 </span>Definition of basis invariance</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider any eigenspace spanned by ground truth eigenvectors <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\psi_{j},\psi_{j+1},\dots\psi_{j+k-1}]=V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\psi_{j},\psi_{j+1},\dots\psi_{j+k-1}]=V</annotation></semantics></math>. Also recall that, by Spectral Theorem, we can decompose any vector <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> into a linear combination of all eigenvectors:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=\sum_{i=1}^{n}c_{i}\psi_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=\sum_{i=1}^{n}c_{i}\psi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then a loss function is basis invariant if any rotation of the projected component <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="VV^{\top}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">VV^{\top}u</annotation></semantics></math> does not change the loss incurred by <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> gets to arbitrarily “choose" with what basis it wants to express its <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="VV^{\top}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">VV^{\top}u</annotation></semantics></math> component. Sign invariance is a special case of basis invariance, where changing sign is equivalent to rotating over a one-dimensional subspace (note that this is slightly stronger than the most apparent form of sign invariance, where we would say <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(u)=\mathcal{L}(-u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(u)=\mathcal{L}(-u)</annotation></semantics></math>; instead, we can flip any <span id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">component</span> <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}\psi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}\psi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> when decomposed in terms of eigenvectors).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Basis invariance)<span id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider an eigenspace spanned by ground truth eigenvectors <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\psi_{j},\psi_{j+1},\dots\psi_{j+k-1}]=\Psi\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\psi_{j},\psi_{j+1},\dots\psi_{j+k-1}]=\Psi\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider an eigenspace rotation <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\Psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\Psi}</annotation></semantics></math> defined as such:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\Psi}=\Psi A\Psi^{\top}+(I_{n}-\Psi\Psi^{\top}),A\in\textsc{SO}(k)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">SO</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\Psi}=\Psi A\Psi^{\top}+(I_{n}-\Psi\Psi^{\top}),A\in\textsc{SO}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A loss function <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(u)</annotation></semantics></math> is basis invariant if, for all such <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi,R_{\Psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi,R_{\Psi}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(u)=L(R_{\Psi}u)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(u)=L(R_{\Psi}u)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.3.2 </span>Proofs</h4>

<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Energy loss is basis invariant)<span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\Psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\Psi}</annotation></semantics></math> and a single eigenvector prediction <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\top}Lu=(R_{\Psi}u)^{\top}L(R_{\Psi}u)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\top}Lu=(R_{\Psi}u)^{\top}L(R_{\Psi}u)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">First note that <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\Psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\Psi}</annotation></semantics></math> is orthogonal; the set of all <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\Psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\Psi}</annotation></semantics></math> describes a subset of <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SO(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SO(k)</annotation></semantics></math> where only the <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> basis vectors in <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> are rotated. Thus, we have <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\Psi}^{\top}R_{\Psi}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\Psi}^{\top}R_{\Psi}=I</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">In addition, because <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> is an eigenspace, all columns are eigenvectors with a shared eigenvalue <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\Psi}L=\Psi A\Psi^{\top}L+L-\Psi\Psi^{\top}L=\lambda\Psi A\Psi^{\top}+L-\lambda\Psi\Psi^{\top}=L\Psi A\Psi^{\top}+L-L\Psi\Psi^{\top}=LR_{\Psi}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\Psi}L=\Psi A\Psi^{\top}L+L-\Psi\Psi^{\top}L=\lambda\Psi A\Psi^{\top}+L-\lambda\Psi\Psi^{\top}=L\Psi A\Psi^{\top}+L-L\Psi\Psi^{\top}=LR_{\Psi}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\Psi}^{\top}LR_{\Psi}=R_{\Psi}^{\top}R_{\Psi}L=L" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\Psi}^{\top}LR_{\Psi}=R_{\Psi}^{\top}R_{\Psi}L=L</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, for any <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\top}Lu=u^{\top}R_{\Psi}^{\top}LR_{\Psi}u=(R_{\Psi}u)^{\top}L(R_{\Psi}u)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\top}Lu=u^{\top}R_{\Psi}^{\top}LR_{\Psi}u=(R_{\Psi}u)^{\top}L(R_{\Psi}u)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Eigenvector loss is basis invariant)<span id="Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\Psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\Psi}</annotation></semantics></math> and a single eigenvector prediction <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and ground truth eigenvalue <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert Lu-\lambda u\rVert=\lVert L(R_{\Psi}u)-\lambda(R_{\Psi}u)\rVert" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert Lu-\lambda u\rVert=\lVert L(R_{\Psi}u)-\lambda(R_{\Psi}u)\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We know, from our proof above in Lemma 1, that <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\Psi}L=LR_{\Psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\Psi}L=LR_{\Psi}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Because <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\Psi}\in\textsc{SO}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">SO</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\Psi}\in\textsc{SO}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert R_{\Psi}x\rVert=\lVert x\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert R_{\Psi}x\rVert=\lVert x\rVert</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert Lu-\lambda u\rVert=\lVert R_{\Psi}(Lu-\lambda u)\rVert" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert Lu-\lambda u\rVert=\lVert R_{\Psi}(Lu-\lambda u)\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert Lu-\lambda u\rVert=\lVert L(R_{\Psi}u)-\lambda(R_{\Psi}u)\rVert" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert Lu-\lambda u\rVert=\lVert L(R_{\Psi}u)-\lambda(R_{\Psi}u)\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We have an even stronger statement of invariance for energy loss: <span id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">given a predicted set of <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> orthogonal vectors, rotating the vectors within the same subspace does not impact loss. </span>In other words, a model trained on energy loss only needs to predict the correct <span id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">subspace</span> of <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> eigenvectors. This is clearly not true of eigenvector loss. Depending on the application, this kind of invariance can be good or bad.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Energy loss is rotation invariant)<span id="Thmlemma3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> be a Laplacian matrix and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be some <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional subspace. Suppose <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=[u_{1},u_{2},\dots,u_{k}],W=[w_{1},w_{2},\dots,w_{k}]\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=[u_{1},u_{2},\dots,u_{k}],W=[w_{1},w_{2},\dots,w_{k}]\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times k}</annotation></semantics></math> are both orthonormal bases for <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{k}\Tr(U^{\top}LU)=\frac{1}{k}\Tr(W^{\top}LW)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{k}\Tr(U^{\top}LU)=\frac{1}{k}\Tr(W^{\top}LW)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that <math id="Thmlemma3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="UU^{\top}=WW^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">UU^{\top}=WW^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, as they are both orthogonal projectors for the same subspace. Then we have, by the cyclic property of trace:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{k}\Tr(U^{\top}LU)=\frac{1}{k}\Tr(UU^{\top}L)=\frac{1}{k}\Tr(WW^{\top}L)=\frac{1}{k}\Tr(W^{\top}LW)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{k}\Tr(U^{\top}LU)=\frac{1}{k}\Tr(UU^{\top}L)=\frac{1}{k}\Tr(WW^{\top}L)=\frac{1}{k}\Tr(W^{\top}LW)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Node feature augmentation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The diffusion operator <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> of a graph <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=D^{-1}A" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=D^{-1}A</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Each entry <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the probability of starting a random walk at node <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and ending at node <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> after one step. One can also take powers of the diffusion operator, <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each entry of the powered matrix, <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{t}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{t}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>, represents the probability of starting a random walk at node <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and ending at node <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> after t steps</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>j</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> wavelet operator <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> of a graph <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{j}=P^{2^{j-1}}-P^{2^{j}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{j}=P^{2^{j-1}}-P^{2^{j}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{0}=I-P" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{0}=I-P</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">A wavelet bank, <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{J}</annotation></semantics></math> is a collection of wavelet operators such that:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{J}=\{\Psi_{j}\}_{0\leq j\leq J}\cup P^{2^{J}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>J</mi></msup></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{J}=\{\Psi_{j}\}_{0\leq j\leq J}\cup P^{2^{J}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Wavelet positional embeddings</span> encode information about the relative position of each node within the graph. We randomly select two nodes from each graph, <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, and start dirac signals <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i},\delta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i},\delta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. We then apply these signals to each wavelet, <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, in our wavelet bank. The wavelet positional embedding for node <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> row of the resulting matrix.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{m,k}=\Psi_{k}(m,\cdot)\begin{bmatrix}|&amp;|\\
\delta_{i}&amp;\delta_{j}\\
|&amp;|\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mtd><mtd><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mtd><mtd><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{m,k}=\Psi_{k}(m,\cdot)\begin{bmatrix}|&amp;|\\
\delta_{i}&amp;\delta_{j}\\
|&amp;|\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{m}=\begin{bmatrix}w_{m,1}&amp;\dots&amp;w_{m,J}\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{m}=\begin{bmatrix}w_{m,1}&amp;\dots&amp;w_{m,J}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Diffused dirac embeddings</span> encode information about the connectedness of each node and its neighbors. For each node, <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, we apply the <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> row of the diffusion matrix <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> to each wavelet <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> in our wavelet bank. As above, the difused dirac embedding for node <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> row of the resulting matrix.</p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{m,k}=\Psi_{k}(m,\cdot)~P(m,\cdot)^{\top}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{m,k}=\Psi_{k}(m,\cdot)~P(m,\cdot)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{m}=\begin{bmatrix}d_{m,1}&amp;\dots&amp;d_{m,J}\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{m}=\begin{bmatrix}d_{m,1}&amp;\dots&amp;d_{m,J}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Uniqueness up to co-spectrality)<span id="Thmlemma4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1},G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1},G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be graphs of size <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> with Laplacian matrices <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1},L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1},L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. Let <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{1}_{m},d^{2}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{1}_{m},d^{2}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the diffused dirac embeddings for each node in <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1},G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1},G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then if <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> have different eigenvalues, <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{d^{1}_{m}:m\leq n\}\neq\{d_{m}^{2}:m\leq n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{d^{1}_{m}:m\leq n\}\neq\{d_{m}^{2}:m\leq n\}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the random-walk Laplacian of a graph: <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{rw}:=I-D^{-1}A=I-P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{rw}:=I-D^{-1}A=I-P</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, note that <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{rw}=D^{-1}L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{rw}=D^{-1}L</annotation></semantics></math>. Observe that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{rw}Dv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{rw}Dv</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=D^{-1}LDv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D^{-1}LDv</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=D^{-1}U\Lambda U^{\top}Dv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D^{-1}U\Lambda U^{\top}Dv</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=Bv\text{ for some diagonalizable matrix }B\text{ with eigenvalues }\lambda_{i},\dots,\lambda_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for some diagonalizable matrix </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> with eigenvalues </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=Bv\text{ for some diagonalizable matrix }B\text{ with eigenvalues }\lambda_{i},\dots,\lambda_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Where <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=\begin{bmatrix}\psi_{1}&amp;\dots&amp;\psi_{n}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=\begin{bmatrix}\psi_{1}&amp;\dots&amp;\psi_{n}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> orthonormal eigenvectors of <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is the diagonal matrix of eigenvalues <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1},\dots,\lambda_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1},\dots,\lambda_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>.
Any change to the eigenspectrum of <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, clearly results in a change to <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{rw}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{rw}</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{0}=I-P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{0}=I-P</annotation></semantics></math>, any two graphs with distinct Laplacian eigenspectra will have distinct diffused dirac node embeddings.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Detailed experimental settings</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A complete overview of model hyperparameters and settings can be found in Table <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ A.5 Detailed experimental settings ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Learning Laplacian Eigenvectors: a Pre-training Method for Graph Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Heuristically, the Graph-level MLP head hidden dimension is chosen to be the max # nodes multiplied by the hidden dimension size of the base GNN. We do NOT omit the trivial eigenvector when counting number of eigenvectors predicted.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>A comprehensive list of all model hyperparameters used during the eigenvector pre-training step. All hyperparameters highlighted in gray are specific to eigenvector-learning, while other listed configs reflect general GNN settings (and are set to match default values in each respective baseline work).</figcaption>
<div id="A1.T4.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:120.2pt;vertical-align:-59.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-277.0pt,96.5pt) scale(0.4,0.4) ;">
